{
  "description": "Page placement (CON-01) and float32 precision (CON-05). CAD->world: d = ((cx-ox)*s, -(cy-oy)*s); world = anchorMm + rot(q, d) with rot(0)=(x,y), rot(1)=(-y,x), rot(2)=(-x,-y), rot(3)=(y,-x). The window's four corners map to a world box [wx0,wy0,wx1,wy1]; widthPt = ceil((wx1-wx0)/mmPerPt - 1e-9), heightPt likewise; widthMm = widthPt*mmPerPt; centerX = wx0 + widthMm/2 (y likewise). World->page: x = (xw-wx0)/mmPerPt, y = heightPt - (yw-wy0)/mmPerPt. Web page->world uses mmPerPt = widthMm/widthPt and the CON-01 formulas. roundingBoundMm r = 0.5*ulp32(max(widthPt,heightPt))*mmPerPt; chordToleranceMm = max(0.1 - r, 0.01). errorMm is the world distance between the exact point and the web's result from the float32 page point.",
